If  $\Delta ABC$  is an isosceles triangle with  $AB=AC=5, BC=6$  and has points  $D, E \in AC$  such that  $AD =1, DE=2, EC=2$ , then the extent (or area) of  $\Delta BDE = S$  computes to: $S = [\Delta ABC] - [\Delta ABD] - [\Delta BEC] = \frac{1}{2}(AB)(BC)sin \angle{B} - \frac{1}{2} (AB)(AD)sin \angle{A} - \frac{1}{2}(BC)(EC)sin \angle{C}$ ;

or  $S = \frac{1}{2}[(5)(6) \cdot (4/5) - (5)(1)(6/5)(4/5) - (6)(2)(4/5)]$ ;

or  $S = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(24 -\frac{24}{5}-\frac{48}{5}\right) = \frac{24}{5}$ ;

or  $15S =$  $\fbox{72}$ .

